infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Where a class type parameter lives: instance vs static
  desc T is bound per instance, so the single class object can never see it
  compares
    - label Instance side — T bound per construction
      children
        - label T solved at construction
          desc new Box(42) infers T = number from the argument
        - label Every method shares one T
          desc A Box<number> can only ever map numbers
        - label Methods add their own U
          desc map<U> introduces a parameter independent of the instance T
        - label T is a per-instance fiction
          desc The checker maintains a separate T for each instance
    - label Static side — one shared class object
      children
        - label Exists before any instance
          desc One Box constructor, shared across every instance
        - label Cannot reference the class T
          desc Static members cannot reference class type parameters
        - label No coherent T to read
          desc Statics span all instances regardless of their T
        - label Fix: give the static its own generic
          desc static of<U>(v: U): Box<U>, solved at the call site
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
